# Story page: inventory
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Satchel
---
Snakes have no pockets, no shoulders and no reason to carry luggage, and yet {name} has a satchel. I have stopped asking how.

I was warned once never to look inside another creature's satchel, just as I was warned never to lend my umbrella to a woman named Marguerite. I heeded only one of those warnings, and I still miss the umbrella.
